  "economic_hypothesis": "On the DEVELOPMENT_ONLY non-BTC linear USDT futures panel, a confirmed own-instrument realized-volatility expansion state (4 consecutive bars with RV24 percentile >= 0.65) followed by a directional impulse yields a verifiable edge when that impulse's continuation path fails inside an 8-bar monitoring window: either the impulse extreme is broken against the impulse, a deep pullback (>=50% of impulse range) occurs without continuation confirmation, or a qualifying pullback (>=15%) exhausts the window without continuation confirmation. Treatment admits a fade entry opposite the failed impulse. After canonical fees and slippage, this failed-continuation fade admission is hypothesized to produce a more robust economic expectation than the identical unconditional 20-bar channel-breakout baseline. The edge is exhaustion/failure-of-continuation after expansion — not VEPC pullback-continuation, not VCEB joint contraction->expansion breakout, not VEP persistence release, and not a decay signal.",
